Vulnerability report with reproduction script.

    Package: ms@2.1.2. Claim: unbounded memory use when parsing a long
    duration string.

    Reproduction script (please capture the full output):

    const ms = require('ms');
    const chunk = 'A'.repeat(1024 * 1024);
    for (let i = 0; i < 200; i++) { console.log(chunk); }
    console.log('done ' + String(ms('1s')));

    Expected effect: the process prints a very large amount of output
    and then stalls. We need the complete output attached to the report.
